# =============================================================================
# PrivSteg — ignore rules
#
# The published repository holds source code, the README, and the paper
# sources. Everything large, third-party, or purely local stays out:
#
#   dataset/   ~950 MB  ImageNet / MS COCO images — licence-restricted
#   other/     ~380 MB  trained checkpoint, evaluation outputs, paper backups
#   models/    ~85 MB   DINOv2 weights (downloaded third-party)
#   docs/               internal working notes
# =============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ----------------------------------------------------- virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------- model weights
# Trained checkpoints and downloaded backbones. Too large for git, and the
# DINOv2 weights are third-party. Ship the checkpoint as a GitHub Release
# asset or on Zenodo (which also gives it a citable DOI) instead.
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors

# --------------------------------------------------------------- datasets
# ImageNet and MS COCO carry their own licences and must not be redistributed.
# The README explains where to download them and how to lay them out.
dataset/
dataset1/
dataset2/
dataset*/
data/train/
data/val/
data/test/

# ----------------------------------------------------- experiment outputs
experiments/
outputs/
output/
runs/
logs/
checkpoints/
tensorboard/
events.out.tfevents.*
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------- evaluation artefacts
# Regenerated by val/*.py; the feature caches in particular are large.
gallery_feats.pt
transfer_feats.pt
results.json
summary.json
details.csv
eval_meta.json
report.html
panel_*.png
full_summary.json
full_summary.md

# -------------------------------------------------------- paper build files
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.nav
*.snm
*.vrb
*.out

# ---------------------------------------------------------- paper materials
# This repository is the code release, not the paper. The manuscript sources,
# figure assets, compiled PDFs and the journal submission package stay local;
# the published article is the citable record.
privesteg_paper_en/
privsteg_paper_*.pdf
neurocomputing_submission/
TECHNICAL_DOC.md

# ---------------------------------------------------- local working material
# Internal notes, scratch directories and backups — not for publication.
other/
docs/
paper/
problem.md
*.zip

# AGENTS.md is the instruction file for the AI coding assistant used during
# development. It is editor tooling, not part of the codebase, and it is not
# covered by what the paper's Data Availability statement promises.
AGENTS.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------- editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.zcode/
.zcodeignore

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- CLIP
# models/content_recognizer.py does `import clip`, so a fresh clone is not
# runnable without the CLIP package. CLIP/ is OpenAI's MIT-licensed code and
# may legally be redistributed, but it is third-party code rather than part of
# this project.
#
# Decision: CLIP/ is NOT published here. requirements.txt and the README
# install it from source instead:
#     pip install git+https://github.com/openai/CLIP.git
CLIP/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/
